{"arrivo":"da","origine":"gml","origine_nome":"Middle Low German","livello2":"non","livello2_nome":"Old Norse","n":7,"parole":[{"parola":"dåre","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"captivate, charm, enchant, fascinate","termine_origine":"dōren","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"dōren","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"dára","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German dōren, derived form the noun. Late Old Norse dára is also borrowed from Low German."},{"parola":"eventyr","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"prestito","incerta":"no","significato":"adventure","termine_origine":"eventǖre","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"eventǖre","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"æfintýr","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"frm","nome":"Middle French","termine":"adventure","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"adventūrus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German eventǖr(e), cognate with German Abenteuer (late Old Norse æfintýr and Swedish äventyr are also from Low German). The word is borrowed from Middle French a(d)venture (hence also English adventure), from Latin adventūra (“things that will happen”), a future participle of the ver"},{"parola":"forskel","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"difference (separating one thing from another)","termine_origine":"vorschel","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"vorschel","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"skilnaðr","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German vorschel (“difference”). Replaced native word skilnad, from Old Norse skilnaðr."},{"parola":"herskab","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"lordship","termine_origine":"herschop","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"herschop","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"hyski","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gmq-oda","nome":"Old Danish","termine":"hærskap","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"herskapr","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"By surface analysis, herre + -skab. From Middle Low German herschop (“lordship, dominion”). The word merged with the native word Old Danish hæskap from Old Norse hyski (“family, household”), hjúskapr. Another possible etymological origin is from Old Danish hærskap, from Old Norse herskapr. Danish: h"},{"parola":"men","pos":"conj|noun","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"but","termine_origine":"men, man","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"men, man","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"meðan","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Chiefly from Middle Low German men, man (“just, but”). To some extent merged with Old Norse meðan (“while”), whence medens, mens."},{"parola":"rast","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a rest, pause, break (during a hike, travel etc.)","termine_origine":"rast","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"rast","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"rǫst","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*rastō","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*ros-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Middle Low German rast. Second definition is from Old Norse rǫst, from Proto-Germanic *rastō, *rastijō (“rest”), from Proto-Indo-European *ros-, *res-, *erH- (“rest”)."},{"parola":"skrumpe","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to shrink, shrivel, dry up, decrease","termine_origine":"schrumpen","catena":[{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"schrumpen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"skreppa","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From a mix of Middle Low German schrumpen and Old Norse skreppa. Related to krympe and skorpe."}]}